  "conclusion": "Both explicit flags cause the renderer to override every MM UUID with a renderer rank and monotonic request counter plus modality/item index. UUIDs propagate into MM hashes and encoder-cache identifiers. Thus the ordinary chat/STT renderer paths cannot reuse content-addressed encoder embeddings across distinct requests under this condition, although EncoderCacheManager and its allocation remain present and can retain/reuse entries within one request.",
